tatement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-factorial-twopow-support"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-factorial-twopow-support"],"id":"long.thm-factorial-twopow-support","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.18 (Factorial-support and $`2^k`$-support instances)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.18, p. 49, label thm:factorial-twopow-support","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For every integer $b\\ge2$, both\n$$\n\\sum_{k\\ge0}\\frac1{b^{(k+1)!}-1}\n \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n \\sum_{k\\ge0}\\frac1{b^{2^k}-1}\n$$\nare irrational. These are instances of the preceding theorem. For the factorial support the preceding least common multiple is $k!$ when $k\\ge1$, so the gap is $k\\,k!$. For the powers of two it is $2^{k-1}$, so the gap is $2^{k-1}$. Both tend to infinity. The conclusion concerns these two supports, not every infinite support.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-factorial-twopow-support","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-factorial-twopow-support","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-factorial-twopow-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_factorial_support%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-factorial-twopow-support%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_factorial_support%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.irrational_erdosSum_factorial_support"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de792